## Final Judgement
Based on the fact-check, the key findings consistently and clearly refute the claim. Major health organizations do not endorse "pox parties" for COVID-19, citing significant risks of severe illness and long-term complications like MIS-C in children. There was no sufficient evidence in late 2020 that natural infection would confer long-lasting immunity needed for herd immunity. Furthermore, the proposal violates fundamental medical ethics, especially concerning vulnerable populations like children, and poses a serious risk of uncontrolled community transmission. Experts at the time uniformly prioritized vaccination over dangerous, uncontrolled infection as the path to herd immunity.

